  "assumption": "DHW and HotSpot errors are bounded by 0.005 in their respective units, as if rounded to nearest 0.01. Public metadata do not establish the original rounding mode. Decimal grid consistency is evidence of granularity, not proof of the assumption.",
  "derivation": "Two DHW endpoints contribute at most 0.005+0.005; each of h outgoing HotSpot contributions can be under-subtracted by at most 0.005/7. Future nonnegative stress cannot erase retained history. Threshold rounding from true HS<1 to displayed HS=1 over-subtracts outgoing stress, making this lower floor conservative.",
